      "source": "Public 8th edition references (American Cancer Society staging summary and standard 8th edition gastric TNM); Medscape staging article was paywalled",
      "provenance": "8th edition gastric adenocarcinoma TNM, rewritten in original wording from criteria published on public references (cancer.org and standard 8th edition gastric staging) after the Medscape article returned a paywall; invasion depths, node counts, and stage mappings preserved exactly. Interim content pending the licensed content and R1 clinical verification.",
      "introduction": "The 8th edition staging system applies to gastric (stomach) adenocarcinoma. The T category reflects depth of invasion through the gastric wall layers, and the N category is defined strictly by the number of involved regional nodes (examination of at least 16, ideally 30 or more, is recommended for accurate pN). Tumors of the esophagogastric junction whose epicenter lies within 2 cm of the junction and extends into the esophagus are staged as esophageal cancers.\n\nA distinctive feature of 8th edition is that it provides separate stage-group tables for clinical (cTNM), pathological (pTNM), and post-neoadjuvant (ypTNM) staging, so the same T/N/M combination can map to different stages depending on the table used. The stage groups listed below are the PATHOLOGICAL (pTNM) groups, in which pN3 is split into pN3a and pN3b; the post-neoadjuvant (yp) table is given separately under postNeoadjuvant and collapses N3 into a single category.",
